<h2>STANDARD 1 YEAR PARTS WARRANTY</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Unless otherwise stated on the sales invoice or listing, eligible parts sold by 417 Motoring LLC are covered by a one (1) calendar year limited warranty beginning on the original date of purchase.</li>
  <li>If a covered part is determined to be defective during the warranty period, 417 Motoring LLC, at its discretion, may provide a replacement part or refund the original purchase price of the covered part. Coverage applies only to the component specifically purchased and does not automatically extend to accessories, sensors, modules, hardware, or other components attached to or included with it.</li>
  <li>As part of a warranty claim, the purchaser may be required to provide diagnostic documentation and/or allow inspection of the allegedly defective component by an independent third party.</li>
  <li>Warranty coverage does not apply to failures resulting from improper installation, incorrect diagnosis, unresolved vehicle fault codes, defective workmanship, abuse, misuse, racing or competition use, modifications, overheating, lack of maintenance, contamination, or operation with incorrect or insufficient fluids or lubricants.</li>
  <li>Diagnostic charges, towing, storage, vehicle rental, loss of use, programming, calibration, shipping, and other incidental or consequential expenses are not covered unless specifically stated in writing.</li>
  <li>417 Motoring LLC is not responsible for injuries, property damage, vehicle damage, or other losses resulting from improper installation, handling, modification, or use of a purchased component.</li>
  <li>Vehicle years, models, and interchange information provided in listings or invoices are intended to assist with identifying compatible applications. Due to manufacturer interchangeability, the donor vehicle's exact year, trim, or configuration may differ from the purchaser's vehicle. The purchaser and/or installer is responsible for confirming proper fitment and interchangeability before installation.</li>
  <li>Labor charges are not included under the standard parts warranty unless separate labor coverage is specifically stated on the purchaser's invoice.</li>
</ul>
<h2>ENGINE WARRANTY TERMS</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Engines must be professionally installed by a properly licensed or certified automotive repair facility. Proof of professional installation may be required for warranty consideration.</li>
  <li>Components attached to the engine are provided for convenience and are not guaranteed or covered unless specifically identified as covered on the invoice. These may include, but are not limited to, intake and exhaust manifolds, turbochargers/superchargers, harmonic balancers, fuel injectors, fuel system components, flywheels/flexplates, brackets, water pumps, alternators, starters, A/C compressors, wiring harnesses, sensors, switches, thermostats, and emissions equipment.</li>
  <li>Prior to installation, the installer must replace or service all applicable maintenance items, including fluids, filters, gaskets, seals, spark plugs, and timing components when required by the manufacturer's recommended installation procedures.</li>
  <li>417 Motoring LLC ships engines and other applicable components with fluids drained. The purchaser and installer are responsible for filling the engine and all related systems with the correct type and quantity of oil, coolant, and other required fluids before operation.</li>
  <li>The cooling system must be inspected, properly filled, and confirmed to be functioning correctly before the engine is operated.</li>
  <li>Overheating, oil starvation, improper lubrication, contamination, improper tuning, incorrect installation, or continued operation after a warning condition may void warranty coverage.</li>
  <li>Disassembly, modification, or unauthorized removal of cylinder heads, internal engine components, or the engine block without prior authorization from 417 Motoring LLC will void the warranty.</li>
</ul>
<h2>TRANSMISSION WARRANTY TERMS</h2>
<ul>
  <li>All applicable seals, gaskets, filters, and fluids should be replaced or serviced before installation.</li>
  <li>Transmissions are shipped with fluids drained. The purchaser and installer are responsible for filling the transmission with the manufacturer's specified type and quantity of fluid before operation.</li>
  <li>Transmission coolers, lines, and related fluid systems must be properly flushed or replaced as necessary to prevent contamination from the previous transmission.</li>
  <li>Required programming, adaptation, relearning, coding, or calibration procedures must be completed according to the vehicle manufacturer's specifications.</li>
  <li>Damage to gears, housings, cases, shafts, or other components resulting from improper installation, insufficient lubrication, abuse, misuse, incorrect programming, or vehicle related problems is not covered.</li>
  <li>Transmission control modules (TCMs), sensors, switches, wiring, and other electronic components included with a transmission are considered ancillary components and are not covered unless specifically stated otherwise.</li>
  <li>Opening, disassembling, modifying, or tampering with a transmission without prior authorization from 417 Motoring LLC will void warranty coverage.</li>
  <li>Fluid leaks, seals, gaskets, and labor expenses are not covered under the standard parts warranty.</li>
</ul>
<h2>AXLES, DIFFERENTIALS, CARRIERS &amp; TRANSFER CASES</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The purchaser and installer are responsible for inspecting and replacing seals, gaskets, and other serviceable components as necessary before installation.</li>
  <li>Seals, brake components, sensors, switches, actuators, and shift motors are not covered unless specifically stated otherwise.</li>
  <li>Components will be shipped with fluids drained. The purchaser and installer are responsible for adding the manufacturer's required lubricant or fluid in the correct quantity before operation.</li>
  <li>Damage caused by insufficient or incorrect fluid, improper installation, abuse, misuse, incorrect gear ratios, or incompatible drivetrain components is excluded from warranty coverage.</li>
</ul>
<h2>SHEET METAL &amp; BODY PARTS</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Used body and sheet metal components are sold in the condition represented in the listing and accompanying photographs.</li>
  <li>Unless specifically stated otherwise, cosmetic imperfections consistent with used automotive components—including scratches, chips, dents, surface corrosion, paint wear, fading, and other normal signs of use are not considered warrantable defects.</li>
  <li>Damage or deterioration resulting from accidents, improper installation, modification, abuse, fire, hail, wind, flooding, environmental exposure, or other external causes is not covered.</li>
</ul>
<h2>AIRBAGS &amp; SUPPLEMENTAL RESTRAINT SYSTEM (SRS) COMPONENTS</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Recycled airbags and other SRS components sold by 417 Motoring LLC are sold AS IS. No standard parts warranty is provided for these components.</li>
  <li>Airbags and SRS components must be inspected and installed by a properly qualified professional in accordance with the vehicle manufacturer's procedures and all applicable laws and regulations.</li>
  <li>SRS systems are safety critical systems. Incorrect installation, programming, handling, storage, or component selection can cause the restraint system to malfunction and may result in serious injury or death.</li>
  <li>The purchaser assumes responsibility for ensuring that any recycled SRS component is appropriate for the intended vehicle and is professionally installed, programmed, and tested as required.</li>
</ul>
<h2>GENERAL WARRANTY REQUIREMENTS</h2>
<p>Warranty coverage applies only to the original purchaser and is not transferable unless otherwise agreed to in writing by 417 Motoring LLC.</p>
<p>The purchaser is responsible for providing reasonable documentation necessary to evaluate a warranty claim, which may include the original invoice, professional installation invoice, diagnostic reports, photographs, videos, fault codes, maintenance records, and other relevant information.</p>
<p>Do not disassemble, modify, repair, or dispose of a potentially defective part before receiving authorization from 417 Motoring LLC. Doing so may prevent us from properly evaluating the claim and may result in denial of warranty coverage.</p>
<p>Any replacement or refund provided under warranty does not restart the original warranty period unless expressly stated otherwise in writing.</p>
<p>Warranty coverage is subject to the specific terms, exclusions, and limitations stated on the original sales invoice or product listing. Where those terms differ from this general policy, the terms specifically provided with the transaction will control to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p>
